  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/4767374/adjunct-clinical-instructor-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Clinical Instructor of Nursing Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Clinical Instructor Job Number PC00055 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 12/19/2024 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Providence College’s baccalaureate program in Nursing is seeking candidates for adjunct clinical faculty positions. The successful candidates will teach clinical in their specialty area, including medical-surgical, pediatric, maternal-child, public health, or psychiatric nursing, at a partner healthcare setting. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences and help shape an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of nursing students. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability to support the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. The adjunct clinical faculty position requires a commitment of 8 hours per week for 14 weeks, for a total of 112 clinical hours, and includes two required orientation days prior to the start of clinical instruction. Compensation for the position is $10,400 Duties and Responsibilities Successful candidates will teach clinical groups in one of the specialty nursing courses at a partner healthcare setting. Adjunct clinical faculty will be responsible for providing clinical instruction, supervision, and evaluation of nursing students in accordance with course and program objectives. The position requires 8 hours per week for 14 weeks, as well as participation in two required orientation days prior to the start of the clinical experience. The two orientation days are included as part of the position’s compensation. Candidates with a master’s degree in nursing and strong clinical skills in nursing are encouraged to apply. Education and Experience Candidates with an earned master’s degree in nursing and a minimum of five years of professional nursing clinical experience in any nursing specialty area are strongly encouraged to apply. Candidates must also have an active, unencumbered license in good standing to practice as a Registered Nurse in Rhode Island or be eligible to apply for such licensure. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu/ . Applicants are asked to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, a statement of teaching philosophy, and three professional references with contact information. Review of applications is ongoing and will continue until the positions are filled. For additional information, please contact Dr. Deborah McManus, Chair of the Department of Nursing, at 401-865-2320 or dmcmanu1@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5454463/assistant-clinical-professor-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Renewable Contingent Faculty Job Number PC00280 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 08/19/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Nursing at Providence College (also referred to as “the College” or “PC”) invites applications for a full-time Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing to join our growing and mission-driven program beginning August 2027. We are seeking an innovative and student-centered educator with expertise in Medical Surgical Nursing who is excited to shape the future of nursing education at PC. The ideal candidate will be able to make meaningful connections between best practices in nursing education, a commitment to the dignity of the whole person, and the Catholic mission and identity of the College. The successful faculty member will play a pivotal role in designing and delivering high-impact clinical experiences that prepare undergraduate nursing students to lead with excellence, compassion, and integrity. They will collaborate closely with an enthusiastic team of faculty and professional staff to advance our cutting-edge teaching and simulation facilities and contribute to a dynamic curriculum that integrates leadership development, evidence-based practice, and holistic patient care. The new faculty member will teach Medical Surgical Nursing I and Medical Surgical Nursing II Clinicals. Clinical Nursing faculty at PC contribute to college and professional service in accordance with expectations for clinical faculty which include teaching excellence and service to the college. If desired, scholarship can also be a component of the role and mentoring in this area is provided through the Department of Nursing. Candidates with an earned master’s and professional clinical training in the medical surgical nursing specialty are strongly encouraged to apply. The Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing will report to the Department Chair and provide high-quality undergraduate clinical instruction. Primary responsibilities include developing, delivering, and assessing clinical courses and experiential learning activities that reflect evidence-based practice and support the mission of Providence College. The medical-surgical faculty member will collaborate closely with simulation, lab, and didactic faculty to ensure alignment between didactic content, skills acquisition, simulation based learning, and clinical application. Because nursing skills, clinical judgment, and patient care concepts are integrated throughout the medical surgical nursing sequence, this faculty member will play an important role in supporting curricular continuity across classroom, lab, simulation, and clinical learning environments. Additional duties include advising undergraduate nursing students, contributing to curriculum development, and participating in departmental and college services such as committee work, program review, and accreditation activities. The faculty member is expected to support students’ professional growth by fostering leadership skills, clinical judgment, and research literacy within a collaborative, student-centered environment. A doctoral degree is required for this faculty appointment. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences as it shapes an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of students entering nursing and other health professions. The 153,000 sq. ft state-of-the-art Ben Mondor Center for Nursing and Health Sciences houses the School of Nursing and Health Sciences’ existing and future undergraduate and graduate programs. This one-of-a-kind facility opened in January 2025 and features the latest classroom design and technologies and showcases expansive clinical simulation and research facilities. A student career education and advising center, along with conference and meeting space, is included as part of the inspiring resources intended for the next generation of healthcare providers, faculty, and staff. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. The salary range for this position is between $80,000-$90,000. Education and Experience Minimum Qualifications: • Master’s degree in nursing required; doctoral preparation preferred. • Unencumbered license as a registered nurse in Rhode Island or eligibility for licensure in Rhode Island; if teaching clinical outside Rhode Island, licensure must be held in the state in which clinical instruction occurs. • Demonstrated expertise in medical-surgical nursing and the ability to support students in applying theory to clinical practice. • Experience in clinical teaching, precepting, mentoring, or supervising nursing students or nurses in a clinical setting. • Ability to support student learning, clinical judgment development, professional formation, and safe patient care in the clinical environment. • Commitment to the mission of the College and to working collaboratively with faculty, students, and clinical partners. Preferred Qualifications: • Doctoral preparation in nursing or a related field. • Prior experience teaching nursing students in clinical, laboratory, simulation, or didactic settings. • Experience with clinical course coordination, student evaluation, remediation, and competency-based assessment. • Familiarity with AACN Essentials, clinical judgment development, NCLEX-RN preparation, and contemporary nursing education standards. • Experience integrating clinical learning with simulation, skills laboratory, and classroom content. • Familiarity with CCNE accreditation standards, program evaluation, and continuous quality improvement processes. • Experience working collaboratively with clinical partners, faculty, and students to support safe, high-quality clinical education. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available), undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Deborah McManus, Nursing Department Chair, at dmcmanu1@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5473287/assistant-professor-of-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00288 Division Academic Affairs Department Biology Opening Date 09/04/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Biology at Providence College in Providence, RI invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level, beginning August 1, 2027. We seek candidates who will hold a Ph.D. in the biological sciences and preferentially post-doctoral experience. Successful candidates are expected to develop and maintain an active research program with original scholarship and to demonstrate excellence in teaching and mentoring of undergraduate students. The successful candidate should be able to teach General Biology for biology majors, as well as one or more upper-level courses in their area of expertise, which may include Physiology, Developmental Biology, or Genetics and Genomics.The department has outstanding teaching and research facilities including a vivarium, a microscopy and bioimaging suite, a cell culture room, a new spinning disc confocal microscope, autoclave, freezers, common use molecular equipment, and dedicated wet labs for student/faculty research. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we encourage applications from candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. Applicants should apply online at the College's career site at https://careers.providence.edu/ and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, and a research statement. In the teaching statement, please include a section titled “ Developing Paths to Student Success” , wherein you discuss your instructional approaches to helping undergraduate students define paths to success in the classroom. In the research statement, please include a section titled “ Conducting Research at a Primarily Undergraduate Institution ” , in which you discuss how you will adapt your research program to the undergraduate-centered focus of Providence College Biology. Review of applications will begin by Nov 1 st , 2026. For additional information please contact: Patrick Ewanchuk, Chair, Biology Department, Providence College, Providence, RI 02918-0001 or ewanchuk@providence.edu . The salary range for this position is between $77,000-$87,000. Education and Experience We seek candidates who will hold a Ph.D. in the biological sciences and preferentially post-doctoral experience. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5474301/assistant-professor-of-accountancy": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accountancy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Accountancy Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00290 Division Academic Affairs Department Accountancy Opening Date 09/08/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Accountancy in the School of Business at Providence College is seeking a full-time, tenure-track faculty member at the rank of assistant professor commencing August2027. Providence College is a nationally recognized institution known for excellence in undergraduate education, a strong liberal arts tradition, and a distinctive Catholic and Dominican mission. Its commitment to academic excellence and student success is reflected in consistent national recognition, including a #2 ranking among Regional Universities in the North inU.S. News & World Report’s 2026 Best Colleges ranking, inclusion inForbes’ Top Colleges for 2026, and recognition as one ofThe Princeton Review’s Best 391 Colleges for 2026. Housed in the Arthur F. and Patricia Ryan Center for Business Studies, the AACSB-accredited Providence College School of Business is a fast-growing and innovative academic community committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and student success. Nationally recognized for its undergraduate programs, the school is consistently ranked among the Top 50 best undergraduate business schools in the nation byPoets&Quants. The city of Providence, Rhode Island, offers an exceptional quality of life, combining the cultural and culinary amenities of a larger city with the accessibility and character of a close-knit community. Known for its acclaimed restaurant scene, vibrant arts and cultural community, historic architecture, and distinctive neighborhoods, Providence is also home to a rich higher education ecosystem, with eight colleges and universities contributing to the city’s intellectual and creative energy. The assistant professor will join the Department of Accountancy , which consists of fourteen(14) full-time faculty members and offers an undergraduate major and minor in accountancy, in addition to courses in accounting for the graduate business program. Position Summary: The assistant professor of accountancy will contribute to the department’s teaching, research, and service missions. We welcome applicants representing a range of perspectives and areas of teaching and scholarship. A Ph.D.in accounting from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. ABDs with anticipated completion by the time of appointment will also be considered. Salary: $130,000-$150,000 Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: The assistant professor will be committed to high-quality teaching and student advising, and will teach six (6)courses during the academic year, across the fall and spring semesters, including undergraduate courses in accounting, and courses at the graduate level as needed. There may also be opportunities to teach during the winter and summer semesters. Research: The assistant professor will be expected to conduct and publish high-quality research in their area of concentration. Maintenance of AACSB Scholarly Academic qualifications is required. Service :The assistant professor will be expected to engage in service activities for the department, school, and college, as well as ongoing practice-oriented activities consistent with AACSB qualification requirements as defined by the School of Business. Education and Experience A Ph.D.in accounting from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. ABDs with anticipated completion by the time of appointment will also be considered. Supplemental Information Please submit your application materials online . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications must be received by 11:59 p.m. EDT on September 15, 2026.Your application must include the following: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Graduate/doctoral transcript(s) Teaching philosophy statement Teaching evaluations summary Research statement outlining current and future research agenda Contact information for three references (for letters of recommendation) Note: References will receive an automated email via NEOED with instructions and a link for uploading their letter of recommendation. Additional documentation may be required from candidates who will be subsequently invited for a campus visit. For questions regarding this position, please contact Search Committee Chair Dr. Christine Earley at cearley@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5476890/administrative-assistant-corporate-and-foundation-relations-planned-and-estate-g": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Corporate and Foundation Relations/Planned and Estate Giving",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Corporate and Foundation Relations/Planned and Estate Giving Salary $29.00 - $31.50 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00296 Division Institutional Advancement Department Corporations and Foundations Opening Date 09/09/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Provide administrative and operational support for the Offices of Corporate and Foundation Relations and Planned and Estate Giving. Manage time-sensitive tasks confidential donor and prospect information, and a wide range of administrative workflows that enable both offices to function efficiently. Duties and Responsibilities Prepare, organize, and maintain departmental records, files and databases including confidential donor, prospect, and gift information. Serve as an internal resource on administrative processes related to gift handling, particularly retirement plan distributions, foundation and corporate grants, and other specialized gift types. Ensure the accuracy, maintenance, and reconciliation of departmental financial accounts, process invoices and credit card payments, prepare transmittal reports and billing, and complete precise, timely data entry within the College's accounts payable system.(35%) Compose and produce correspondence and reports. Perform intermediate and advanced computer functions including managing databases, creating, analyzing, integrating and importing linked spreadsheets, creating mail, envelope, and table merges, creating and editing captions, adding graphics, editing images, footnotes, endnotes, indices, and tables of content. Track and confirm database details of processed gifts to ensure accuracy and maintain donor records within Affinaquest including appropriate contact info and individuals representing corporate and foundation entities. Serve as the primary editor and point of contact for the internal marketing team and external marketing and communications vendors.(20%) Execute acknowledgement processes for gifts and grants, including producing gift receipts and stewarding members of the Harkins Society through personalized correspondence and coordination of annual society events. Engage constituents, prospects, volunteers, and campus partners by phone, email, mail, and in person, address inquiries, book gifts, track internal grant approvals, and support effective communication across both offices.(20%) With supervision, organize and coordinate special projects for Corporate and Foundation Relations, including presentations, foundation site visits, letters of inquiry and grant applications, grant stewardship and impact reports, newsletters, education programs, and special events. Assist with corporation and foundation prospect research using databases and online resources, providing accurate and timely support for fundraising strategies and institutional partnerships.(20%) MARGINAL DUTIES : Answer phones, greet, and direct visitors to appropriate areas or persons. (5%) Perform all other duties as maybe required. Education and Experience Associate's degree from an accredited institution. Three to five years of experience as administrative supporting higher education or advancement, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications and database systems. Knowledge of, or a drive to learn, basic graphic design and the production of marketing materials in accordance with institutional brand guidelines (Adobe, Thank View, e.g.) Strong prioritization skills Ability to take initiative and manage multiple tasks effectively. Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Consistently meets deadlines. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5497495/assistant-coach-high-performance": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach-High Performance",
      "description": "Assistant Coach-High Performance Salary $32.00 - $35.00 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Part-time Staff Job Number PC00315 Division Athletics Department Athletic Administration Opening Date 09/28/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Assistant High-Performance Coach supports the physical development and athletic performance of student-athletes across multiple sport programs. This position assists with the implementation of strength and conditioning programs that promote athletic performance, injury prevention, and overall student-athlete well-being. Responsible for compliance with all NCAA rules and regulations. This is a part-time position, up to 15 hours per week or as needed. Duties and Responsibilities Design, implement, instruct and progress sports specific training programs to college varsity sports teams. Prepare year-round training programs that will enhance the athleticism of student-athletes and reduce injuries. (50%) Prepare speed and agility sessions and pre-practice/competition warm up protocols. Attend assigned team practices, games, and scheduled conditioning sessions. (30%) Perform daily/weekly/monthly equipment maintenance duties as assigned by head coach. (10%) Oversee work study students in the performance of their daily tasks. (10%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree in a Sports Science related field from an accredited institution Two years’ experience in the sports training field at the Intercollegiate level preferred Experience training in a variety of sports First Aid/CPR/AED Certification NSCA and USAWF Certification preferred Strong leadership and motivational abilities Excellent written and communication skills Competent computer literacy skills May be required to travel to campus during inclement weather. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5504054/assistant-professor-of-art-history": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art History",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Art History Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00322 Division Academic Affairs Department Art and Art History Opening Date 10/02/2026 Closing Date 11/1/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Providence College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in the Department of Art and Art History at the assistant professor level, beginning August 1, 2027. We seek an interdisciplinary teacher-scholar who specializes in the chronological era from c.1800 to the present. Salary: $70,000-$80,000 Duties and Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will include courses in Modern and Contemporary Art, participation in a team-taught Survey, advanced undergraduate seminars, and Methods and Senior Thesis courses on a rotating basis. We welcome research and courses that center intersectional approaches to Modern and Contemporary art and media and also may be cross-listed with Women’s and Gender Studies, Black Studies, American Studies, Global Studies, Latin American and Latina/o Studies, Asian Studies, and other departments such as Theatre, Dance, and Film; Communication; English; Political Science, etc., depending on the expertise and interests of the person hired. Cooperation and coordination with our thriving PC Galleries’ exhibitions and programming is also desired. Collegial interaction and engagement with students in our Studio Art program is also important to the position. Education and Experience Preference will be given to applicants who possess a Ph.D. from an accredited institution and demonstrate a strong commitment to innovative teaching, use of technology, interdisciplinary art historical scholarship, and demonstrated broad methodological interests within the field(s) of expertise. The position includes competitive salary and benefits, as well as research support including travel funds, library resources, and grant writing assistance. Supplemental Information Candidates should submit the following documents online: a cover letter; curriculum vitae; graduate transcripts; a statement of teaching philosophy; and the names and email addresses of three reference providers who will be prompted to submit letters of recommendation on your behalf. Providence College’s application system will automatically email the individuals listed as references, asking them to upload their letters of recommendation directly. Applicants are encouraged to have all letters submitted before November 1. Application instructions are available on the College website at: https://careers.providence.edu/ . For additional information or questions, please contact Bing Huang, search chair, Department of Art & Art History, bhuang@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5514170/assistant-director-of-corporate-foundation-relations": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Corporate/Foundation Relations",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Corporate/Foundation Relations Salary $67,000.00 - $73,000.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00342 Division Institutional Advancement Department Corporations and Foundations Opening Date 10/13/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview In collaboration with the Director, solicit corporate and foundation donors in order to meet CFR's fundraising goals. Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the lead solicitor on 20-25 written proposals to private foundations and contribute to additional proposals of which the Director is lead solicitor. Solicit 20-30 corporate partners annually.(65%) Lead all CFR stewardship activities, including the preparation and submission of 15-20 donor reports annually. Coordinate grant reporting requirements and collaborate with campus partners to gather outcomes and financial information. Organize two to four site visits per year. (20%) Develop and implement overall solicitation and stewardship strategies. Assist in managing the CFR prospect portfolio through prospect research, pipeline management, proposal tracking, and deadline monitoring. Serve as the primary point of contact for corporate sponsorship requests and partner with academic liaisons to identify and coordinate corporate engagement opportunities. Oversee CFR engagement events, including the annual corporate partners reception and two to three events at basketball and hockey games.(10%) Promote a culture of grant seeking with faculty and other key campus partners. Work with the Director to develop relationships with campus partners that lead to solicitations. Identify new corporate and foundation prospects and share information with campus partners. Participate in new faculty orientations and other sessions to share information about the services provided by CFR. Maintain internal and external CFR webpages. Attend faculty and administrator lectures and events to achieve broad and deep institutional knowledge and understanding. (5%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as maybe required. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution required. Minimum of three to five years of fundraising or related experience in a higher education setting or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Strong written and verbal communication skills Exceptional interpersonal skills and a strong appreciation for teamwork Proficiency with MS office suite Strong organizational skills and the ability to multi-task Experience with Salesforce/Affinaquest software system or an equivalent CRM system a plus Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
