    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5451933/assistant-professor-of-chemistry-and-biochemistry": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry and Biochemistry Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00274 Division Academic Affairs Department Chemistry and Bio-Chemistry Opening Date 08/18/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Providence College in Providence, Rhode Island, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the areas of analytical chemistry, experimental physical chemistry, or biochemistry, with a preference for an interdisciplinary combination thereof, beginning August 1, 2027. A Ph.D. in chemistry or biochemistry or related fields is required, and postdoctoral or equivalent experience is highly encouraged. We are seeking candidates in the teacher-scholar model who are committed to engaged learning and collaborative, original research with undergraduate students, who employ inclusive practices in undergraduate teaching, and who will participate in the wider life of the Department and the College. Successful applicants will be expected to teach lecture and laboratory courses at the introductory level, two lecture or lab courses between analytical chemistry, physical chemistry, and biochemistry, and elective courses in their subdiscipline. A willingness to teach courses in the core curriculum or for non-majors is also valued. The teaching load at PC is nine credits per semester; research with undergraduate students may count in load under certain conditions. Candidates are expected to train and mentor undergraduates in the research laboratory and to establish an active, externally funded research program involving our students. Our science facilities recently underwent a major renovation/expansion, giving us a contemporary space for teaching and research. The position will come with an office, research space, and start-up funds. The Department is especially interested in applicants who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community through their research, teaching, and/or service obligations. Applicants are encouraged to include in their cover letter and teaching statement evidence of effective engagement with diverse audiences. Applicants should complete the online application form at https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, undergraduate and graduate transcripts (copies are acceptable for application purposes), a description of research plans involving undergraduates (2-3 pages, plus a list of required instrumentation and equipment), a teaching statement that should include their philosophy on teaching, mentoring, and managing research at a primarily undergraduate institution, and the names and contact information for three references. Qualified applications received by October 1 st , 2026 will be guaranteed consideration. The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry is accredited by the ACS and its biochemistry degree is also accredited by the ASBMB. Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission . Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found here . The salary range for this position is between $77,000-$87,000. Education and Experience MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: PhD in chemistry, biochemistry, or related fields PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Postdoctoral experience Supplemental Information For additional information, please contact: Dr. Seann Mulcahy, Chair, Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, Providence College, Providence, RI 02918-0001, or smulcahy@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5454363/assistant-professor-of-nursing-medical-surgical": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing – Medical Surgical",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Nursing – Medical Surgical Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00278 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 08/19/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Nursing at Providence College (also referred to as “the College” or “PC”) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Nursing to join our growing and mission-driven program beginning August 2027. We are seeking an innovative and student-centered educator with expertise in Medical Surgical Nursing who is excited to shape the future of nursing education at PC. The ideal candidate will be able to make meaningful connections between best practices in nursing education, a commitment to the dignity of the whole person, and the Catholic mission and identity of the College. The successful faculty member will play a pivotal role in designing and delivering high-impact didactic, and experiential learning experiences that prepare undergraduate nursing students to lead with excellence, compassion, and integrity. They will collaborate closely with an enthusiastic team of faculty and professional staff to advance our cutting-edge teaching and simulation facilities and contribute to a dynamic curriculum that integrates leadership development, evidence-based practice, and holistic patient care. The new faculty member will teach Medical Surgical Nursing I and II and may also teach other courses within the BSN curriculum such as Fundamentals/Health Assessment, Complex Nursing Problems, or NCLEX Prep depending upon qualifications, interest, and needs of the department. Nursing faculty at PC maintain an active scholarly agenda and contribute to college and professional service in accordance with expectations for tenured and pre-tenured faculty. Candidates with an earned doctorate and advanced professional training in nursing are strongly encouraged to apply. The tenure-track Assistant Professor of Nursing will report to the Department Chair and provide high-quality undergraduate instruction. Primary responsibilities include developing, delivering, and assessing courses and experiential learning activities that reflect evidence-based practice and support the mission of Providence College. The medical-surgical tenure-track faculty member will collaborate closely with simulation, lab, and clinical faculty to ensure alignment between didactic content, skills acquisition, simulation-based learning, and clinical application. Because nursing skills, clinical judgment, and patient care concepts are integrated throughout the medical-surgical nursing sequence, this faculty member will play an important role in supporting curricular continuity across classroom, lab, simulation, and clinical learning environments. Additional duties include advising undergraduate nursing students, contributing to curriculum development, and participating in departmental and college services such as committee work, program review, and accreditation activities. The faculty member is expected to maintain an active scholarly agenda consistent with tenure expectations and to support students’ professional growth by fostering leadership skills, clinical judgment, and research literacy within a collaborative, student-centered environment. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences as it shapes an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of students entering nursing and other health professions. The 153,000 sq. ft state-of-the-art Ben Mondor Center for Nursing and Health Sciences houses the School of Nursing and Health Sciences’ existing and future undergraduate and graduate programs. This one-of-a-kind facility opened in January 2025 and features the latest classroom design and technologies and showcases expansive clinical simulation and research facilities. A student career education and advising center, along with conference and meeting space, is included as part of the inspiring resources intended for the next generation of healthcare providers, faculty, and staff. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. The salary range for this position is between $95,000-$105,000. Education and Experience Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing (e.g., Ph.D., DNSc, or DNP). Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor or Professor; demonstrated experience in teaching at the collegiate level. Advanced professional preparation and clinical expertise in the areas of Medical Surgical Nursing. Unencumbered license as a registered nurse or eligibility for licensure as a registered nurse in Rhode Island. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with curriculum development, revision, and program assessment in nursing education. Experience integrating simulation, clinical laboratory, and experiential learning into nursing curricula. Familiarity with CCNE accreditation standards, program evaluation, and continuous quality improvement processes. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Deborah McManus, Nursing Department Chair, at dmcmanu1@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. A doctoral degree is required for this faculty appointment. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5458959/assistant-professor-of-health-sciences": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Health Sciences Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00282 Division Academic Affairs Department Health Sciences Opening Date 08/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Health Sciences , in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences (SNHS) at Providence College (also referred to as “the College” or “PC”), seeks to fill two tenure-track assistant professor positions to begin in the Fall 2027 (i.e., August) semester. We are seeking applicants with teaching, research, and/or clinical practice experience in the health and/or human biological sciences. The successful candidate will have primary teaching responsibilities across the Health Sciences curriculum which serves undergraduate students in the health sciences, nursing, and related majors preparing for health-related careers. Sample areas of teaching may include human anatomy & physiology, microbiology for the health professions, nutrition science, exercise science, and/or upper-level elective courses in the applied health sciences depending on the candidate’s interests and expertise. Faculty are expected to maintain an active scholarly agenda and contribute professional service in accordance with the College’s expectations for pre-tenured faculty. Applicants with an earned doctorate in health sciences, physiology, biology, or a closely related field are strongly encouraged to apply. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences and shape an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of students entering nursing and other health professions. The 153,000 sq. ft state-of-the-art Ben Mondor Center for Nursing and Health Sciences houses the School of Nursing and Health Sciences’ existing and future undergraduate and graduate programs. This one-of-a-kind facility opened in January 2025 and features the latest classroom design and technologies and showcase expansive clinical simulation and research facilities, including a human performance laboratory and environmental chamber. The department features a purpose-built classroom for teaching microbiology for the health professions and courses on applied human biology. A student career education and advising center, along with conference and meeting space, is included as part of the inspiring resources intended for the next generation of healthcare providers, faculty, and staff. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae , teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Todd Olszewski, Health Sciences Department Chair, at tolszews@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on September 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A doctoral degree is required for this faculty appointment. The salary range for this position is between $80,000-86,000. Duties and Responsibilities This tenure-track faculty position will report to the Chair of the Department of Health Sciences. Primary teaching responsibilities will be at the undergraduate level and will include the development, implementation and assessment of curriculum, student advising, service to the college. Education and Experience Candidates with an earned doctorate with teaching and research experience in health sciences, applied human physiology or biology, or a closely related field are strongly encouraged to apply. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, graduate transcript, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Todd Olszewski, Health Sciences Department Chair, at tolszews@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on September 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A doctoral degree is required for this faculty appointment. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5468545/assistant-professor-of-political-science": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00286 Division Academic Affairs Department Political Science Opening Date 09/01/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Political Science Department at Providence College invites applications for a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level in the field of European Politics , grounded in perspectives from either International Relations or Comparative Politics , with additional expertise in research methods , particularly quantitative research methods . The field of European Politics is understood broadly by our Department, and we welcome applicants across a wide range of methodological and substantive interests. We seek candidates with demonstrated expertise in quantitative research design and statistical analysis who can contribute to the Department's research methods curriculum. Substantive areas of specialization may include, for example, European integration and governance; the European Union and its institutions; democratization and democratic backsliding; political parties, elections, and public opinion; migration and citizenship; comparative political institutions; political economy; colonial and postcolonial politics (particularly with Asia and Africa); identity, nationalism, and populism; security and foreign policy; environmental and climate politics; gender and social policy; or other Europe-centered topics. Geographically, we welcome candidates whose research focuses on any region or country within Europe, including cross-national and comparative perspectives with countries in other regions. Successful candidates will be expected to maintain an active research agenda, teach undergraduate courses in their area of specialization and introduction courses in Political Science or International Relations/Comparative Politics, and contribute to the Department's core curriculum in research methods, including quantitative methods and statistics. The ability to engage students in empirical political analysis and to mentor undergraduate research is especially valued. Candidates should possess a PhD or evidence of completing their PhD by the expected hiring date. Review of applications will begin on October 1 and will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: Applicants should possess a Ph.D. in political science (or be very close to completion) and will be asked to demonstrate evidence of the potential for teaching excellence, strong research skills, and potential for continued research productivity. Apply online at https://careers.providence.edu where you will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, names and contact information of three references, teaching materials, and one or more samples of scholarly writing, either published or unpublished. For additional information, please contact Dr. Casey Stevens, chair of the search committee, at csteven3@providence.edu or Dr. Ruth Ben-Artzi, department chair, at rbenartz@providence.edu. NOTE: search committee members will be hosting optional informational interviews at APSA in Boston, and prospective applicants who wish to schedule an informational interview during the conference are encouraged to contact us no later than August 20. Those unable to attend the conference may contact Dr. Stevens to schedule a remote informational interview. Deadline: For full consideration, your completed application should be submitted no later than October 1, 2023. Review of applications will commence as they are received and will continue until the position is filled. We anticipate completing on-campus interviews by December 11 and making a final decision by early January 2027. Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission . Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found here . Download PDF reader. The salary range for this position is between $70,000-$80,000. Education and Experience Applicants should possess a Ph.D. in political science (or be very close to completion) and will be asked to demonstrate evidence of the potential for teaching excellence, strong research skills, and potential for continued research productivity. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5474320/assistant-professor-of-management": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Management Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00291 Division Academic Affairs Department Management Opening Date 09/08/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Management in the School of Business at Providence College is seeking a full-time, tenure-track faculty member at the rank of assistant professor commencing August 2027. Providence College is a nationally recognized institution known for excellence in undergraduate education, a strong liberal arts tradition, and a distinctive Catholic and Dominican mission. Its commitment to academic excellence and student success is reflected in consistent national recognition, including a #2 ranking among Regional Universities in the North in U.S. News & World Report ’s 2026 Best Colleges ranking, inclusion in Forbes ’ Top Colleges for 2026, and recognition as one of The Princeton Review ’s Best 391 Colleges for 2026. Housed in the Arthur F. and Patricia Ryan Center for Business Studies, the AACSB-accredited Providence College School of Business is a fast-growing and innovative academic community committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and student success. Nationally recognized for its undergraduate programs, the school is consistently ranked among the Top 50 best undergraduate business schools in the nation by Poets&Quants . The city of Providence, Rhode Island, offers an exceptional quality of life, combining the cultural and culinary amenities of a larger city with the accessibility and character of a close-knit community. Known for its acclaimed restaurant scene, vibrant arts and cultural community, historic architecture, and distinctive neighborhoods, Providence is also home to a rich higher education ecosystem, with eight colleges and universities contributing to the city’s intellectual and creative energy. The assistant professor will join the Department of Management , which consists of twelve (12) full-time faculty members and offers an undergraduate major in management, in addition to courses in management for the graduate business program. The assistant professor of management will contribute to the department’s teaching, research, and service missions. We welcome applicants representing a range of perspectives and areas of teaching and scholarship, with a particular interest in those whose work engages with teams, organizational behavior, and related micro-organizational research. A Ph.D. in management, organizational behavior, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. ABDs with anticipated completion by the time of appointment will also be considered. Salary: $120,000-$135,000 Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: The assistant professor will be committed to high-quality teaching and student advising, and will teach six (6) courses during the academic year, across the fall and spring semesters, including undergraduate courses in management and courses at the graduate level as needed. There may also be opportunities to teach during the winter and summer semesters. Research: The assistant professor will be expected to conduct and publish high-quality research in their area of concentration. Maintenance of AACSB Scholarly Academic qualifications is required. Service: The assistant professor will be expected to engage in service activities for the department, school, and college, as well as ongoing practice-oriented activities consistent with AACSB qualification requirements as defined by the School of Business. Education and Experience A Ph.D. in management, organizational behavior, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. ABDs with anticipated completion by the time of appointment will also be considered. Supplemental Information Please submit your application materials online . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. For full consideration, applications must be received by 11:59 p.m. EDT on September 25 , 2026 . Your application must include the following: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Graduate/doctoral transcript(s) Teaching philosophy statement Teaching evaluations summary Research statement outlining current and future research agenda Contact information for three references (for letters of recommendation) Note: References will receive an automated email via NEOED with instructions and a link for uploading their letter of recommendation. Additional documentation may be required from candidates who will be subsequently invited for a campus visit. For questions regarding this position, please contact Search Committee Chair Dr. Matthew Eriksen at meriksen@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5475873/assistant-professor-of-elementary-special-education": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Elementary / Special Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Elementary / Special Education Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00293 Division Academic Affairs Department Elementary and Special Education Opening Date 09/09/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Elementary/Special Education Department at Providence College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Elementary Special Education, beginning in Fall 2027. We seek a scholar and educator who will contribute to the department’s commitment to academic excellence, evidence-based instructional practices, and the preparation of highly effective elementary and special education teachers. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring undergraduate teacher candidates, scholarship and professional engagement, and collaboration with schools and community partners. We particularly welcome candidates with an established or emerging research agenda that has the potential to enhance the department’s national visibility and contribute meaningfully to the field of elementary education, teacher preparation, and/or special education as an inclusive model. Founded in 1917, Providence College (PC) is a premier Catholic liberal arts institution steadfastly committed to academic excellence through a dynamic core curriculum, a distinctive Development of Western Civilization Program, and abundant experiential learning opportunities. The only U.S. higher education institution administered by the Dominican Friars, PC is committed to providing a variety of opportunities for intellectual, social, moral, and spiritual growth in a supportive environment. Providence College believes that cultural and intellectual pluralism is essential to the excellence of its academic programs and strives to foster an academic culture and campus community reflecting the global environment in which we live and work. The approximately 105-acre campus is situated in Rhode Island’s capital city and is close to the many cultural and educational offerings of Rhode Island’s “renaissance city.” Additionally, Providence is located an hour from Boston and just a few hours from New York City. For years, Providence College has been recognized #1 in the U.S. News & World Report “Regional Universities – North Category” and is ranked #1 in Undergraduate Teaching. The School of Education and Social Work: The Department of Elementary Special Education is situated within the School of Education and Social Work (SESW). The School of Education and Social Work’s vision statement is that “Our graduates cultivate human flourishing and foster a more just society.” The SESW values Reflection, Inclusivity, Engagement and Excellence. https://education-social-work.providence.edu/ The Elementary/ Special Education Department: The Department of Education is widely recognized for its merged dual certification elementary and special education program. We seek to: a) educate and inclusively prepare outstanding pre-service teacher candidates in both elementary education (grades k-6) and special education (grades k-8); b) engage in high-quality teaching, scholarship, and service; and c) engage in diverse partnerships within our local community, across Rhode Island, throughout the New England Region and Internationally. The Elementary Special Education Program has a long history of emphasizing inclusive education, collaboration, and evidence-based practices. Salary: $69,000-$79,000 Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach face-to-face undergraduate education courses in a merged elementary and special ed department. Design, develop, and deliver high-quality instructional materials, learning experiences, and assessments. Advise Elementary/Special Education majors on coursework, including requirements within the Providence College Core Curriculum. Establish and maintain collaborative relationships with local schools and community partners. Contribute to accreditation and continuous program improvement activities. Participate actively in departmental and College-wide service and committee work. Develop and sustain a productive program of scholarly inquiry and disseminate research through appropriate professional and scholarly venues. Contribute to the College’s strategic priorities and mission through teaching, scholarship, service, and engagement with the broader community. Education and Experience Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in special education, elementary education, language and reading, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. ABD candidates may be considered, provided the doctorate is completed by the time of employment. Demonstrated record of, or clear potential for, scholarly activity and research related to special education, teacher preparation, or a closely related field. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and teacher preparation. Strong interpersonal, communication, and collaborative skills. Prior experience teaching students with disabilities in inclusive settings, including supporting the multi-tiered systems of supports (MTSS) process and IEP development Preferred Qualifications Experience with curriculum development, accreditation, program assessment, or other forms of academic program leadership. Experience teaching undergraduate students, particularly in teacher preparation programs. Experience collaborating with K–8 schools, districts, community organizations, or other educational partners. Evidence of engagement with evidence-based instructional practices and contemporary issues in elementary education. Supplemental Information For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 1, 2026. Instructions to candidates : Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at https://careers.providence.edu and submit the following: Cover letter outlining qualifications Curriculum vitae Teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness Graduate transcripts Three letters of recommendation. If selected for an on-campus interview, candidate will be asked to respond to the college’s Mission Statement For additional information about the position, please contact Dr. Laura Hauerwas, Elementary/Special Education Department, Providence College, Providence, RI 02918-0001 , at lhauerwa@providence.edu NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5477506/assistant-professor-theatre-generalist": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Theatre Generalist",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Theatre Generalist Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00295 Division Academic Affairs Department Theatre, Dance and Film Opening Date 09/10/2026 Closing Date 11/20/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Theatre, Dance and Film at Providence College seeks a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Theatre beginning August 1, 2027. The department seeks a Theatre Generalist with a PhD in Theatre, Theatre History, Dramatic Literature, or a related field. The position includes a 3/3 course load which will include Theatre Appreciation, Script Analysis, History of Theatre, Multicultural Theatre in America, Western Drama in Performance, and special topics courses within the candidate’s expertise. Other courses may include Oral Communication, Oral Interpretation, Introduction to Acting, Public Speaking, Theatrical Production, or Principles of Playwriting, depending on the candidate's expertise. Other duties include participation in departmental mainstage productions, meetings, and activities; new student recruitment; academic advisement; and advisement on student creative projects. Active engagement in creative and/or scholarly work, a commitment to excellence in teaching, and service to the college and one’s discipline are required. Successful candidates will provide evidence of inclusive pedagogy and a commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. The department offers a BA in theatre and theatre with a concentration in musical theatre, as well as minors in dance and film. In addition to the major courses, the department also serves the college by offering courses which fulfill the college’s Fine Arts core requirement and Oral Communication core proficiency. For additional information on the composition of the department, please visit https://theatre.providence.edu/ . The Department of Theatre, Dance & Film is committed to fostering an inclusive community that embraces students, faculty, and staff of all backgrounds and enables them to achieve success. Salary: $66,000-$76,000 Education and Experience Required Qualifications: • An PhD in Theatre, Theatre History, Dramatic Literature, Performance Studies, or a related field (ABD considered if degree is completed by start date) • Evidence of effective teaching at the college/university level • Record of creative and/or scholarly work or evidence of potential for developing future creative and/or scholarly projects • Commitment to teaching, scholarship, advising, and service as integral components of faculty work Supplemental Information Applications for this position are due on November 20, 2026. Application instructions are available at https://careers.providence.edu/ . Submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, graduate transcript(s), and the names and email addresses of three references who can submit a letter of recommendation. For additional information please contact: Megan Chang, Chair, Department of Theatre, Dance, & Film, Providence College, Providence, (401)865-2437 or mchang@providence.edu or Ali Boyd, Academic Coordinator, ali.boyd@providence.edu . NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5482241/assistant-professor-of-philosophy": {
