    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5311087/clinical-supervisor-pact": {
      "title": "Clinical Supervisor - PACT",
      "description": "Clinical Supervisor - PACT Salary $1,320.00 - $5,280.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Adjuncts Job Number PC00222 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 04/16/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview PACT seeks mission-driven professionals to serve as clinical supervisors who mentor, observe, and support secondary teacher candidates placed in Catholic schools. This adjunct role plays a vital part in forming new teachers through coaching, evaluation, and ongoing professional formation. The Providence Alliance for Catholic Teachers (PACT) Program is a two-year, full-time cohort experience for recent college graduates pursuing secondary teaching careers. The program provides comprehensive professional, academic, and spiritual formation while candidates serve as full-time teachers in Catholic schools. PACT is a member of the University Consortium for Catholic Education (UCCE) . Duties and Responsibilities PACT clinical supervisors guide, coach, and evaluate PACT candidates as part of the Internship courses. Clinical supervisors establish positive working relationships with partner school administrators, complete three formal observations during the semester (observations include the observation, conference, and written feedback), and provide ongoing coaching to candidates. As PACT's 'eyes' in the field, clinical supervisors represent the program and communicate with PACT leadership as needed. This position includes the following additional expectations as part of the PACT faculty: Participation in faculty meetings, as necessary Participation in ongoing program improvement efforts Education and Experience Master’s degree in education Minimum of three years of successful secondary-level teaching experience Demonstrated experience in Catholic school settings and alignment with mission Ability to provide formative, actionable feedback that advances teaching and learning Supplemental Information Application review will begin immediately and will continue until an adequate pool is developed. Clinical supervisors must be available during the school day to meet with administrators and conduct observations. In particular, PACT is seeking clinical supervisors to serve in the Roman Catholic Diocese of Burlington, VT. Compensation is based on the number of candidates supervised per semester. Qualified persons should apply online and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, transcript(s), and three letters of recommendation. Application instructions are available at: For further information, please contact Chris Keavy, PACT Director, at ckeavy@providence.edu. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5450549/associate-director-for-alumni-relations": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Associate Director for Alumni Relations Salary $88,000.00 - $93,000.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00271 Division Institutional Advancement Department Alumni Relations Opening Date 08/17/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Serve as a key strategic partner in the planning and implementing of engagement programs to attract different constituencies with the goal of strengthening connections to the college and fostering sustained philanthropic support, with an emphasis on volunteer leadership and class-based engagement. Duties and Responsibilities Develop and oversee the execution of all reunion programming with the goal to engage alumni through their milestone celebration with the college. Collaborate with the Class Giving team throughout the year to achieve program goals including volunteer recruitment and onboarding, training to ensure volunteers are equipped to invite their classmates to participate in reunion programming and contribute philanthropically, and coordination of efforts with prospect managers. Provide year-round support to class committee volunteers and serve as the point of contact for all reunion classes to establish meaningful programming that aligns with the interests of each class while maintaining a strong focus of bringing alumni back to campus. Oversee the reunion budget and implement strategies to generate revenue to offset expenses. Work with the College Events staff and the Marketing and Communications team on all logistics and communications for programming throughout the year and at the culminating Reunion Weekend. Ensure Advancement Services is included throughout to ensure a process for data both before, during, and post-weekend. (40%) Serve as Advancement lead for Homecoming, one of the college’s signature programs with the priority focus of bringing alumni back to campus and engaging them with current College priorities. Co-lead the program with a member of the College Events staff and work in tandem throughout the year-long planning to ensure both Advancement and Institutional goals are established and met each year. Manage the Homecoming budget and designate funding for various departmental programming. Collaboration includes but is not limited to Late Night Madness, engagement and stewardship for donor recognition, admission, student activities, and residential life. Oversee the core committee and campus partners groups, and partner with Marketing & Communications to develop a comprehensive communication and marketing plan that is customized to engage different audiences (students, faculty/staff, parents/families, alumni, and friends). Enlist the support of Advancement Services to ensure a data process is in place to capture a multi-faceted weekend. Collaborate with Athletic partners to capitalize on athletic opportunities and other activities to showcase programs and enhance participant experience. Identify ways to engage the entire PC community and oversee the execution of the weekend. (25%) Provide essential leadership and guidance to direct report(s) to maximize productivity, set performance standards, individual metrics, and routine evaluation of goals. Provide on-going training of staff to ensure strength of skills and a clear understanding of advancement. Meet regularly to ensure prioritization of workload, strong communication and relationship development, and achievement of program goals. (20%) Further the development of a pipeline of alumni volunteers including expansion and management of the class ambassador program, support of volunteer pathways tied to Reunion, Homecoming, and engagement efforts and work closely with the National Alumni Council, serving as a staff liaison and supporting a designated committee to advance alumni engagement priorities. (15%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Represent Alumni Relations through participation in campus-wide committees and cross-functional initiatives. Partner with colleagues across Alumni Relations and Advancement to support alignment of volunteer efforts that advance engagement and philanthropic outcomes. Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution required Five to seven years’ experience in a progressively responsible development fundraising environment or an equivalent combination of education and experience Excellent interpersonal, oral, written communication, and organizational skills Must be proactive, creative, problem-solver and have the ability to interact with a broad range of constituents, including alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of the College Computer proficiency and a demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team Supervisory experience preferred Evenings and weekends required Possible travel Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5451098/director-of-advancement-marketing-communications": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement Marketing & Communications",
      "description": "Director of Advancement Marketing & Communications Salary $100,000.00 - $105,000.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00273 Division VP of Administration and Board Relations Department Marketing and Communications Opening Date 09/11/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Manage, coordinate, and execute strategy and the related creative development and production of digital and print communications supporting the College's development, alumni relations, and engagement efforts. Duties and Responsibilities Conceptualizes, coordinates, and develops robust, multi-channel marketing campaigns from idea to execution, to ensure the achievement of goals related to all fundraising initiatives, in addition to programs, events, services, and outreach to alumni, as well as parents, friends, and other constituents. Working with colleagues within Marketing & Communications, especially the assistant director, and in collaboration with advancement personnel, take the lead responsibility in overseeing conceptualization and creation of print and digital pieces relative to development initiatives and major events including Homecoming Weekend, Reunion, and Friars Give, along with all other events and communications meant to engage alumni. (25%) Lead efforts to ensure that the marketing and messaging needs of the Office of Institutional Advancement are identified, prioritized, coordinated and fulfilled in ways that help achieve goals and optimize the use of resources. Work closely with leaders to develop shared clarity on priorities and messaging imperatives and then activate the Marketing and Communications resources to create the associate materials, often in the context of multiple concurrent projects, all with tight deadlines. Manage expectations and logistics by ensuring that all involved are communicating emerging needs, programmatic changes, and evolving expectations. (20%) Lead collaborations among marketing and communication and advancement colleagues, and freelance associates, to ensure quality, creativity, and effectiveness of college brand-consistent materials supporting advancement initiatives across all channels, including print, web, email, digital ads, video, media, and social media. Identify and implement new and emerging techniques and technologies that will be useful in achieving strategic goals. Use data and metrics to track the effectiveness of these efforts and adjust--often in real time--to ensure better outcomes. (20%) Supervise the assistant director, graduate assistant, and the digital marketing team. Coordinate with other leaders in Marketing & Communications to maximize the use of resources and ensure that deadlines are met. (10%) Manage effective coordination of responsibilities and processes to ensure appropriate marketing and communications support for the College’s comprehensive campaign. Assess the current practices and collaborations, working with leaders in advancement, to support the campaign. Facilitate the culture of greater self-service in advancement, where MarCom provides templates, guidance, and support for use by advancement personnel in creating certain routine communications pieces, e.g. presentation slides, certificates, and event signs. Work with advancement leaders to assess overall structures with the goal of determining continual optimal collaboration. (15%) Serve as the division's point person in the assessment, implementation, and use of technology platforms the College employs for advancement-related marketing, messaging, event management, and data organization. Responsible for contract oversight, as applicable, and for providing marketing and communications expertise for college-wide assessment of new and updated operations systems and processes. (10% MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution required Minimum of five years’ experience in high-output, creative services operation or an equivalent combination of education and experience Superb writing skills and storytelling, applicable to both print and digital formats Demonstrated high level of creativity, exemplified by the ability to conceptualize and create successful multi-channel, coordinated marketing campaigns Ability to lead and inspire others Proven capacity to foster effective collaboration in a high-demand, professional environment, especially across functional units. Advanced understanding of contemporary marketing techniques and delivery systems, e.g. Customer Relationship Management platforms and digital marketing. Significant background in market research and the use of data to guide decision-making Significant experience in a higher education or other advancement communications environment Demonstrated experience in creating print and digital pieces that serve as elements of integrated messaging campaigns and initiatives Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5453936/associate-or-full-professor-of-health-sciences-associate-dean": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean",
      "description": "Associate or Full Professor of Health Sciences; Associate Dean Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00277 Division Academic Affairs Department School of Nursing and Health Sciences Opening Date 08/19/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The School of Nursing and Health Sciences (SNHS) at Providence College (also referred to as “the College” or “PC”) invites applications for the position of Associate Dean of Health Sciences (also called “Associate Dean”) at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. The anticipated start date is August 2027, with the possibility of a January 2027 or spring 2027 start if applicable. The Associate Dean serves as a key member of the School’s leadership team and works closely with the Dean to advance the academic mission of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. Reporting directly to the Dean, the Associate Dean provides leadership in academic affairs, including collaborating directly with the department chairs and program directors to ensure curricular and research excellence and operational effectiveness across the School. The Associate Dean has a particular focus and advises the Dean on matters related to existing and new academic programs, faculty development, student success, and long-term strategic priorities to advance the school’s growth and academic reputation of excellence in the health sciences. The successful candidate will hold a faculty appointment with primary teaching responsibilities in Health Sciences, while collaborating with faculty in Nursing and related majors focused on preparing students for careers in the health professions. Additional opportunities exist to develop new and innovative graduate programs in health sciences. As a tenured faculty member, the successful candidate will maintain an active program of scholarship consistent with their discipline, as well as mentor health sciences faculty to develop their scholarly goals and accomplishments. An additional exciting opportunity is for the Associate Dean to develop new health sciences and interdisciplinary research opportunities and collaborative ventures across the school and college to advance the scholarly reputation of Providence College as a leader in health sciences and health care innovation. The successful candidate will contribute meaningful professional and institutional service in accordance with the expectations of Providence College. Applicants with an earned doctorate in Health Sciences, Exercise Science, Human Physiology, or a closely related field are strongly encouraged to apply. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences and shape an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of students entering nursing and other health professions. The 153,000 sq. ft state-of-the-art Ben Mondor Center for Nursing and Health Sciences houses the School of Nursing and Health Sciences’ existing and future undergraduate and graduate programs. This one-of-a-kind facility opened in January 2025 and features the latest classroom design and technologies and showcase expansive clinical simulation and research facilities, including a human performance laboratory and environmental simulation chamber. The department features a purpose-built classroom for teaching microbiology for the health professions and courses on applied human anatomy and physiology using the latest virtual cadaver technologies. A student career education and advising center, along with conference and meeting space, is included as part of the inspiring resources intended for preparing the next generation of healthcare providers, researchers, and educators. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. The salary for this position is between $125,000-$150,000. Duties and Responsibilities This is a tenure-track faculty position with an administrative appointment as Associate Dean. Essential administrative responsibilities associated with the Associate Dean role report directly to the Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. Faculty responsibilities, including teaching, scholarship, student advising, assessment, and departmental service, report to the Chair of the Department of Health Sciences. Primary teaching responsibilities will be at the undergraduate level and will include academic advising and service to the College. Education and Experience Candidates with an earned doctorate in Health Sciences, Exercise Science, Human Physiology, or a closely related field are encouraged to apply. A doctoral degree, demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, and evidence of scholarly productivity are required for this faculty appointment. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae , teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Todd Olszewski, Health Sciences Department Chair, at tolszews@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5458939/clinical-assistant-professor-of-health-sciences": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Health Sciences Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Renewable Contingent Faculty Job Number PC00281 Division Academic Affairs Department Health Sciences Opening Date 08/24/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Department of Health Sciences , in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences (SNHS) at Providence College (also referred to as “the College” or “PC”), seeks to fill a clinical assistant professor position to begin in the Fall 2027 (i.e., August) semester. We are seeking applicants with teaching and/or clinical practice experience across the broad health sciences and health careers continuum. Areas of particular interest include applied nutrition, health administration, and/or health communications. The successful candidate will have primary teaching responsibilities serving undergraduate students in the health sciences, nursing, and related majors preparing for health-related careers. Successful candidates will also have the opportunity to participate in the department’s team-taught senior seminar in health sciences and develop and teach advanced elective courses in their area of interest and specialization. Department, college, and professional service contributions are required according to the college’s expectations of non-tenure track, clinical faculty. This is an exciting and historic opportunity to join PC’s newly established School of Nursing and Health Sciences and shape an innovative, interdisciplinary curriculum for the next generation of students entering nursing and other health professions. The 153,000 sq. ft state-of-the-art Ben Mondor Center for Nursing and Health Sciences houses the School of Nursing and Health Sciences’ existing and future undergraduate and graduate programs. This one-of-a-kind facility opened in January 2025 and features the latest classroom design and technologies and showcase expansive clinical simulation and research facilities, including a human performance laboratory and environmental chamber. The department features classrooms/labs for teaching microbiology for the health professions and anatomy and physiology using virtual cadavers. A student career education and advising center, along with conference and meeting space, is included as part of the inspiring resources intended for the next generation of healthcare providers, faculty, and staff. As the student body at Providence College grows increasingly diverse, we have a strong preference for candidates who demonstrate a deep commitment to and proven ability in supporting the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups. Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae , teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, undergraduate and graduate transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Todd Olszewski, Health Sciences Department Chair, at tolszews@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A masters or doctoral degree is required for this faculty appointment and demonstrated excellence in teaching at the college level is preferred. The salary range for this position is between $78,000-$82,000. Duties and Responsibilities This tenure-track faculty position will report to the Chair of the Department of Health Sciences. Primary teaching responsibilities will be at the undergraduate level and will include the development, implementation and assessment of curriculum, student advising, service to the college. Education and Experience Master’s or doctoral degree in a health-related discipline. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated expertise in nutrition, population or community health, healthcare systems, and/or health policy. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at: https://careers.providence.edu and submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness, graduate transcript, and three letters of recommendation. For additional information, please contact Dr. Todd Olszewski, Health Sciences Department Chair, at tolszews@providence.edu . Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. A doctoral degree is required for this faculty appointment. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5459121/complex-director": {
      "title": "Complex Director",
      "description": "Complex Director Salary $40,842.00 - $43,343.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00283 Division Student Affairs Department Residence Life Opening Date 08/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Serves as a accessible resource whose core, curriculum-based responsibilities are underscored by reinforcing ethics, responsible conduct, and moral accountability. Work collaboratively with various departments on campus to create opportunities for, and to engage students in, dialogue, personal development, academic achievement, and identity formation. This is a 10 month position. Duties and Responsibilities Participate in the fall, winter, and spring training sessions for the RA’s; supervise, hire, train, and evaluate performance of assigned RA’s and provide feedback and encouragement to RAs for personal and paraprofessional growth. Manage and process RA administrative reports such as weekly reports, duty logs, duty schedules, and incident reports. Meet regularly with the RA’s both individually and in weekly staff meetings. Supervise and evaluate performance of at least one Graduate Hall Director; provide feedback and encouragement to Graduate Hall Director’s personal and professional growth; and meet regularly with Graduate Hall Director to review current concerns and questions. (25%) Maintain up-to-date knowledge and clear understanding of the regulations outlined in the Student Handbook, as well as related legal regulations. Enforce all applicable regulations as needed, communicate behavioral expectations to students through periodic floor and building meetings with complex residents, and conduct judicial conferences of referred cases for students documented for policy violations. Complete and submit infraction reports to the appropriate central staff member. Develop strategies to reduce inappropriate behavior in the complex. Serve as a member of the on-call rotation team for the campus responding to incidents as they arise, following College and Residence Life and Housing protocol, and submitting required documentation. Conduct Brief Motivational Interview alcohol interventions as assigned. Serve as an on-duty member of the Administrator on-call team for the campus. Assist with the administration of the Advocate incident report processing system. Assist with CARE student follow-up and administrative support in Advocate. (20%) Foster, develop, and maintain a sense of community and belonging with assigned complex. Be accessible to residents by being available and visible in the complex. Become aware of, and respond to, residents' needs, interests, and concerns and make appropriate referrals to other College offices. Assist resident assistant staff in implementing community cultivation curriculum and attend individual building and floor meetings whenever possible. Support, attend, and evaluate resident assistant outputs, ensuring that all RAs meet responsibility requirements and ensure they meet the residential community needs. Manage the complex programming budget, provide an accounting of all programming expenses, and supporting documents to Residence Life and Housing. Coordinate and lead departmental administrative projects, including professional development for students and professional staff, housing operations initiatives, and residential programming. (30%) Assume responsibility for the daily operation of one or more residence halls in the campus community. Keep the central staff leadership informed about area activities, emergencies, and other issues of significance. Assist in annual housing selection process and periodic room changes. Serve on the departmental and department-directed committees and task forces. Oversee the periodic building inventories and make appropriate requests for furniture and equipment, maintenance/cleaning work requests, and periodic replacement of appliances and furniture. Perform fire, health, and safety inspections/drills. (25%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree in a related field from an accredited institution required. Master’s Degree preferred. Minimum of two years of full-time experience in a related field or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated understanding of Catholic and/or Christian higher education institutions’ structure, mission, and values Demonstrated experience in the areas of supporting underrepresented students and staff, curriculum development and implementation, facilities management, staff training and/or development, crisis intervention, and student conduct. Ability to manage complex situations and multiple responsibilities simultaneously, mixing long-term projects with urgent or immediate demands. Must exhibit good time management skills and ability to prioritize. Capacity to manage stress and maintain personal and emotional stability in a demanding work environment. Must possess good fiscal management skills and sound judgment. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5467790/clinical-counselor-substance-use-counselor": {
      "title": "Clinical Counselor/Substance Use Counselor",
      "description": "Clinical Counselor/Substance Use Counselor Salary $60.00 - $65.00 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Part-time Staff Job Number PC00285 Division Student Affairs Department Personal Counseling Opening Date 09/04/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Provide individual clinical services to students coping with co-occurring substance use/addiction and mental health concerns. This is a 9 month academic year part-time position. Duties and Responsibilities Provide direct counseling for students and student athletes. Assess level of substance use and mental health concerns. Provide intervention, treatment and referrals. Assess range of mental health symptoms, substance misuse/abuse/addiction symptoms and behaviors. Provide referral of students to off campus resources, higher levels of care, detox, and assist with medical leave requests. Provide substance use assessment and treatment plans to student athletes who test positive on NCAA drug tests. Provide follow-up with students involved in substance use emergencies requiring emergency intervention. Coordinate care as needed. Provide substance use/harm reduction group therapy options to interested students. (35%) Assess students’ emotional, psychological, behavioral, substance use, and developmental mental health concerns which impact current level of functioning. Conduct extensive clinical interviews/assessment/consultation to formulate appropriate treatments plans. Coordinate off-campus psychiatric and/or medical evaluations when necessary and referrals to both on and off campus resources. (30%) Provide substance use assessment and treatment plans to student athletes who test positive on NCAA drug tests. Provide follow-up with students involved in substance use emergencies requirement emergency intervention. Coordinate care as needed. Provide substance use/harm reduction group therapy options to interested students. Connect and consult with psychiatric and other health care providers. Refer to on and off campus professionals when appropriate. (15%) Provide crisis intervention for students who are experiencing acute emotional distress as a result of varying emergencies such as trauma (i.e. security assault), death, substance misuse, or who are a danger to themselves (i.e. suicidal thoughts) or are a danger to others. Determine severity of presenting crisis, degree of danger, level of harm to oneself or others; assess appropriate interventions necessary, coordinate on and off campus assistance with support services. Provide psychological/clinical judgment when required to administration, including the Executive Director of Personal Counseling, AD of Substance Use Services, and the Office of the Vice President. (10%) Complete documentation of clinical and case management encounters within a strict timeline. Maintain records and clinical information consistent with professional standards and PCC practices. Ensure readiness of documentation for in-office psychiatry referrals. (10%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Master’s degree in mental health counseling, clinical social work, or clinical psychology required. One to three years’ experience post-licensure provision of individual clinical services or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience in emergency mental health assessment and crisis intervention, substance use assessment, and disordered eating screenings. Experience providing ongoing care to individuals coping with substance use disorders and mental health diagnoses. Experience working with young adult populations, preferably within a college mental health setting. Ability to work independently clinically while still participating as part of a team. Experience with diverse cultural backgrounds and identities such as BIPOC, LGBTQIA+, first generation students, neurodiverse students, and student athletes. Intermediate experience with electronic medical record software. Basic experience with Microsoft Office Suite and Adobe. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5485770/emergency-medical-technician": {
      "title": "Emergency Medical Technician",
      "description": "Emergency Medical Technician Salary $25.00 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Seasonal Job Number PC00304 Division Student Affairs Department Public Safety Opening Date 09/17/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Under the direction and supervision of the Associate Vice President/Chief of Public Safety or his designee provide emergency medical care to ensure professional medical coverage of students, during hours when the Student Health Center is closed, as well as provide coverage for faculty/staff and visitors of Providence College. Duties and Responsibilities Provide emergency care to the student population on campus to include triage, treatment and stabilization of patients according to RIDPH protocols and Providence College EMS Policies and Procedures. (40%) Complete all documentation as appropriate to all emergency calls. Report any and all incidents, problems, and unusual circumstances to the EMS Chief and the Office of Public Safety on-duty Supervisor when indicated. (10%) Provide follow-up with students who required emergency care during the previous shift via phone call to address any questions or concerns the student may have (weekend shifts only). (5%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Maintain inventory of EMS supplies and ensure all response equipment is adequately stocked. (5%) Participate in and assist with training requirements for Public Safety Officers to include CPR and First Aid Training. (5%) Participate in and assist with training for the Faculty and Staff of Providence College as needed or requested. (5%) Participate in training exercises, including but not limited to tabletop and full-scale practical exercises, as needed. (5%) Provide EMS coverage for on-campus events as requested (College Events, Club Sports). (5%) Be available to work at least 2 weekend shifts per month, as well as a minimum of 4 shifts per month. (Weekend shifts are considered, Friday night, Saturday day and night, Sunday day and night as well as Holidays.) (5%) EMTs will provide support and guidance to any Student EMT Employees in the event they are covering any on-campus event. (5%) Conduct monthly inspections of College AED Units and Naloxone deployments and assist Residence Life with similar training. (5%) Perform all other duties as maybe required. (5%) Education and Experience EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE REQUIRED: Rhode Island EMTA license. Valid CPR certificate Mental Health First Aid Certificate Maintain a valid driver’s license Two to three years pre-hospital care required. High school graduate or equivalent Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Ability to safely operate college EMS vehicles for emergency response. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about Ability to lift and move patients as required to provide pre-hospital care. use of co-ed facilities and living quarters during the required tour of duty. DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5487803/crossings-project-manager-curatorial-assistant": {
      "title": "Crossings Project Manager & Curatorial Assistant",
      "description": "Crossings Project Manager & Curatorial Assistant Salary $35.00 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Temporary Staff Job Number PC00308 Division Academic Affairs Department PC Galleries and Exhibitions Opening Date 09/18/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview PC Galleries (PCG) seeks a temporary, part-time Project Manager & Curatorial Assistant to support CROSSINGS: Wilderness Journeys through Art, Care, and Community, a grant-funded initiative supported by the Creative Arts Collective for Christian Life & Faith. This position is for the duration of the project period, from October 18, 2026, through June 30, 2027. This position will average approximately 22 hours per week. Working under the direction of the Director & Chief Curator and in collaboration with PCG staff, the Project Manager & Curatorial Assistant position serves as a central point of coordination among the project's artists, lenders, campus collaborators, community partners, and grant-funded consultants. The position manages assigned exhibition and program logistics throughout the initiative, including project schedules, meetings, documentation, communications, curatorial research, and the development of interpretive and project materials, as well as other duties as assigned. Duties and Responsibilities Curatorial and Exhibition Production Support: Provide curatorial and community engagement research support under the direction of the Director & Chief Curator, including: Research and compile artist, artwork, lender, bibliographic, and contextual information needed for exhibition development and interpretation. Contribute research and draft materials for exhibition texts, interpretive materials, digital resources, and other public-facing content. Maintain exhibition checklists and organize artwork information, images, captions, credits, permissions, and related exhibition documentation. Support correspondence and coordination with participating artists, galleries, lenders, and other project contributors. Coordinate information and deadlines with exhibition design, lighting, fabrication, and other project specialists. Support exhibition planning and implementation in collaboration with PCG staff as assigned. Programs, Publications, and Engagement: Assist with planning and implementation of project meetings, information sessions, workshops, and related engagement activities. Provide public programming coordination for the CROSSINGS opening, symposium, and related public programs, including schedules, participant information, travel arrangements, program materials, and other logistical needs. Coordinate production deadlines for the Crossings Reflection Guide. Support communication and scheduling with campus and community partners in coordination with the Director & Chief Curator and Community Liaison/Partner Facilitator. Communications, Documentation, and Evaluation Support: Gather and organize project information, images, credits, schedules, and other materials for marketing and communications use. Coordinate scheduling and project access for photography, videography, interviews, and other documentation activities. Support the Evaluation Consultant by coordinating access to project information, schedules, participants, attendance information, and evaluation materials. Assist with organizing project documentation and media for final reporting, archival purposes, and submission to Providence College's Digital Commons. Education and Experience Master's degree in art history, museum studies, curatorial studies, arts administration, visual arts, humanities, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Professional experience in a museum, gallery, arts organization, higher education environment, or related cultural setting. Demonstrated experience coordinating exhibitions, programs, projects, or other complex collaborative initiatives. Strong organizational and project-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple schedules, deadlines, and workstreams. Demonstrated research, writing, editing, and information-management skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, establish priorities, and collaborate effectively within a project team. Proficiency with standard workplace productivity, file-sharing, and collaborative project-management tools (MS-Office, Teams). Supplemental Information Individual must be able to work occasional weekends and evening hours within the approved hours available. Cover letter required with submission. Applicants selected for interview will be required to submit a writing sample (2 pages maximum, derived from an project description, press release or published article) as part of the selection process NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5515226/associate-vice-president-of-enrollment-management": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President of Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Associate Vice President of Enrollment Management Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00343 Division Executive Vice President Department Admissions Opening Date 10/14/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Providence College seeks a strategic, innovative, collaborative, and mission-driven leader to serve as its Associate Vice President of Enrollment Management. The successful candidate will provide institution-wide leadership for undergraduate and graduate enrollment planning, student recruitment, admission, and financial aid, while working across the university to develop coordinated marketing, recruitment, and retention strategies. The Associate Vice President will serve as the institution’s chief enrollment officer. This senior leader will shape and execute a comprehensive enrollment strategy that advances the institution’s mission, supports a diverse and talented student body, strengthens student success, and aligns enrollment decisions with institutional priorities and long-range financial sustainability. The Associate Vice President will bring sophisticated analytical capacity, sound judgment, deep knowledge of admission and financial aid, and the ability to translate market intelligence into clear institutional action. The role requires a leader who can build trust across divisions, communicate effectively with senior administration and the Board of Trustees, and foster a high-performing enrollment organization. The Associate Vice President will be expected to balance aspiration with disciplined execution, preserving the personal character of the Providence College experience while positioning the university to respond to a rapidly changing enrollment environment. Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer, the Associate Vice President of Enrollment Management provides leadership for enrollment planning, recruitment, admission, and financial aid. The position works collaboratively across the college to develop and execute marketing, recruitment, and retention strategies. Core responsibilities include the following: Enrollment Planning and Strategy Create an enrollment planning model for use in annual planning and budget development by appropriate college offices. Develop, articulate, implement, and assess recruitment and enrollment plans for the undergraduate and graduate programs. Analyze current enrollment and retention issues and recommend strategies that connect admission decision-making, student success, and resource stewardship. Examine institutional policies and practices affecting enrollment and retention and present recommendations to senior leadership. Establish performance indicators and regular reporting that support transparent, evidence-informed decision-making. Admission and Recruitment Provide strategic and operational leadership for undergraduate and graduate admission and recruitment. Exercise responsibility for admission decisions, including decisions involving student-athletes, in compliance with applicable NCAA rules and regulations. Approve initiatives that support recruitment programs and services. Guide recruitment market planning, prospective student engagement, application generation, application review, yield, and enrollment conversion. When appropriate, maintain direct engagement in recruitment and application review to remain closely connected to prospective students, families, counselors, and the work of the admission team. Financial Aid Supervise and support the Executive Director of Financial Aid. Oversee the distribution of academic merit scholarships and the strategic implementation of institutional financial aid for eligible students. Connect financial aid decisions to admission, retention, access, and net revenue goals. Monitor institutional financial aid expenditures and ensure that approved resources are not exceeded. Assess the effectiveness of financial aid strategies and recommend adjustments based on enrollment outcomes and institutional priorities. Retention and Cross-Campus Partnership Coordinate the development of recruitment and retention plans with academic and administrative partners. Identify opportunities to improve the quality, clarity, coordination, and responsiveness of services provided to students. Build productive relationships across academic affairs, student affairs, athletics, finance and business, marketing, institutional research, and other areas essential to enrollment success. Marketing and Communications Work collaboratively with marketing colleagues to ensure that recruitment and admission strategies are consistent with the college’s mission and institutional positioning. Guide the development of integrated communication plans that engage students and families through appropriate channels and technologies. Use market insight and audience research to strengthen messaging, recruitment campaigns, and enrollment conversion. Organizational Leadership and Fiscal Stewardship Lead, supervise, and develop senior enrollment staff and promote effective collaboration across the enrollment organization. Manage the office’s operating budget, approve expenditures, and align resources with strategic priorities. Foster an organizational culture characterized by professionalism, service, accountability, innovation, and continuous improvement. Ensure appropriate policies, processes, technologies, and staffing structures are in place to support enrollment goals. Communication, Governance, and Representation Report enrollment strategies, initiatives, results, and recommendations to senior administration and the Strategic Planning Committee of the Board of Trustees. Participate in the Academic Affairs Executive Council, the Marketing Committee, and other institutional bodies relevant to enrollment, retention, and planning. Provide updates on student recruitment initiatives and seek informed recommendations on admission and financial aid matters. Represent Providence College professionally with prospective students and families, school counselors, professional organizations, and other external constituencies. Reporting Relationships The Executive Director of Financial Aid reports to this position. The Associate Vice President also manages a group of eight to ten senior enrollment staff and works closely with leaders and teams across the college whose responsibilities intersect with recruitment, financial aid, retention, marketing, analytics, student success, athletics, and institutional planning. For the full position profile and salary range information, please review the Associate Vice President of Enrollment Management (Chief Enrollment Officer) Profile by clicking here . Education and Experience The successful candidate will be a strategic, ethical, and collaborative enrollment leader with the experience, judgment, and interpersonal skills to engage effectively with students and families, faculty and staff, senior administrators, trustees, alumni, coaches leading Division I athletic programs, and other internal and external partners. The candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to Providence College’s Catholic and Dominican mission, enrollment excellence, student success, and the responsible stewardship of institutional resources. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field from an accredited institution. At least ten years of progressive experience in college or university admission, enrollment management, financial aid, or an equivalent combination of relevant training and experience. Demonstrated expertise in enrollment management and undergraduate and graduate recruitment. Strong leadership, team-building, and organizational management skills. Knowledge of market trends and leading practices in admission and financial aid. Strong analytical and quantitative skills, including the ability to use data, research, and information technology to make decisions and deploy resources. Demonstrated ability to connect the strategic use of financial aid with admission, retention, and net revenue objectives. Exceptional written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Experience using contemporary communication technologies and social media in recruitment. A demonstrated commitment to building a welcoming community and recruiting students from a broad range of backgrounds. Leadership Attributes Strategic and forward-looking Mission-driven and ethically grounded Analytical and evidence-informed Collaborative and relationship-centered Decisive, accountable, and operationally disciplined Innovative, adaptable, and attentive to emerging market conditions Student-centered and committed to service excellence An effective communicator who can build shared understanding across constituencies Supplemental Information Procedure for Candidacy All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as separate documents, a curriculum vitae or resume and a letter of interest addressing the themes in this profile. Application materials should be submitted using Providence College’s online candidate portal and selecting the green “Apply” button located on the top-right hand corner of the job posting. Candidates will be considered until an appointment is made. For priority consideration, applicant materials should be submitted by November 23, 2026. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5359159/practitioner-in-finance": {
      "title": "Practitioner in Finance",
      "description": "Practitioner in Finance Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Renewable Contingent Faculty Job Number PC00246 Division Academic Affairs Department Finance Opening Date 05/29/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The School of Business at Providence College is seeking a practitioner faculty member in finance to begin in the Fall 2026 semester. A practitioner is defined as a full-time contract faculty member who has specialized and significant training, knowledge, skills, competencies, and experience in a particular field relevant to a departmental or programmatic need. The successful candidate for this position will be expected to teach introductory-level and intermediate-level undergraduate courses in finance, including in the areas of financial markets and investments. The successful candidate will also be expected to engage in practice-oriented activities consistent with the standards of AACSB, and to engage in service activities for the school and the college. The salary range for the position is $96,000 - $101,000. Education and Experience A minimum of a master’s degree in finance, or a related field, from an AACSB-accredited institution is required. Supplemental Information Interested persons should apply online by June 5, 2026. All online applications must include the following: Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Graduate Transcript (3) Letters of Recommendation Additional documentation may be required from candidates who will be subsequently invited for a campus visit. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Ed Szado ( eszado@providence.edu ). NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5428853/sr-associate-athletic-director-health-performance": {
      "title": "Sr. Associate Athletic Director Health & Performance",
      "description": "Sr. Associate Athletic Director Health & Performance Salary $150,000.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00267 Division Athletics Department Sports Medicine Opening Date 08/13/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Ensure the comprehensive well-being of student-athletes across physical, mental, and nutritional dimensions. Provide administrative oversight along with direct service delivery, aligning with the institution’s mission to foster holistic athlete development. Duties and Responsibilities Recruit, train, and supervise athletic training staff ensuring high standards of practice and professional development. Assign administrative duties to optimize departmental efficiency. Hold regular meetings of the training staff to ensure proper communication and development. Improve methods and incorporate new technology and teachings into practice. Maintain accurate medical records for all student-athletes, ensuring compliance with regulations. Serve as NCAA healthcare administrator. Provide direct medical care, within the scope of the position, to student athletes in support of other Athletic Trainers. (40%) Serve as the Chief Medical Officer for student-athletes. Oversee and serve as the primary liaison to external Physicians, Orthopedists, specialists, and professional service contracts that work with student athletes. Work with the General Counsel to ensure appropriate licensing and paperwork is completed. Ensure compliance with NCAA regulations, institutional policies, and best practices. Collaborate closely with internal staff and external medical partners to maintain high standards of athlete health, safety, and care. (15%) Serve as the primary athletic department liaison to the Personal Counseling Center. Collaborate with the sports psychology service staff and other members of the center to develop and implement comprehensive mental health and wellness strategies. Manage the budget and oversee programming/events related to health and wellness services. Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of wellness programs, adjusting as necessary. (15%) Serve as a member of the Athletic Director’s executive staff to assist in strategic decision making and provide organizational leadership within the athletic department. Participate in shaping the department’s vision, polices, and long-term goals. Provide input on major decisions such as budget allocation, staffing, and program improvements. Effectively collaborate with other departmental leaders, including the AD, coaches, and support staff, to ensure cohesive operations. Work in conjunction with the AD and Associate AD for Men’s and Women’s Basketball to ensure medical aspects of all NIL contracts are being met. (15%) Supervise the Assistant Athletic Director of Performance Nutrition ensuring alignment with departmental goals, including hiring, training, and fostering professional development. Oversee the Assistant AD in effective and efficient use of the Canavan Sports Medicine Fund, including procurement of supplies and overseeing the fueling station. (7.5%) Oversee the Director of High Performance and their team. Ensure communication between the high-performance staff and the rest of the medical team. Hold regular meetings involving all Health & Wellness constituents to ensure collaboration across all areas. (7.5%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Master’s degree in athletic training from an accredited institution required. Five to seven years’ experience in athletic health and well-being or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Combination of specialized clinical, administrative, and interpersonal skills to effectively manage student-athlete health, performance, and overall wellness. Ability to bring staff together and implement new and creative ideas. Athletic Trainer Certification (ATC) Rhode Island Training Licensure First Aid/CPR Certification Basic proficiency with Health Roster Ability to work weekends and evenings Willingness to travel Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
