    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5451982/student-accounts-specialist-part-time": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Specialist-(Part-time)",
      "description": "Student Accounts Specialist-(Part-time) Salary $23.50 - $26.54 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Part-time Staff Job Number PC00275 Division Finance and Business Department Financial Services Opening Date 08/18/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Provide administrative support to the Bursar’s Office/Student Accounts in the day-to-day operations of the office. This is a part-time position with approximately 25 hours per week. Duties and Responsibilities Manage the Bursar and Refund email inboxes by responding to student and departmental inquiries in a timely and professional manner. Review, process, and post student refund requests accurately to student accounts while ensuring compliance with institutional policies and procedures. Process monthly invoice payments to Brinks, verify billing accuracy, and maintain appropriate documentation to support timely payment processing and account reconciliation. (40%) Provide front office coverage as needed, particularly during lunch periods and staff absences, to ensure uninterrupted customer service. Answer and direct incoming phone calls, process and distribute incoming and outgoing mail, and assist students, parents, faculty, and other visitors with inquiries and requests. Deliver professional, courteous, and efficient support while maintaining a welcoming and service-oriented office environment (35%) Monitor and maintain petty cash funds, ensuring accurate accountability, security, and compliance with established financial policies and procedures. Perform cash and check reconciliation by verifying, posting, and endorsing payments accurately and in a timely manner. Research and resolve discrepancies, maintain detailed financial records, and support audit and reporting requirements to ensure the integrity and accuracy of cash-handling operations. ( 25%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience High School education or equivalent. One to three years of related experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Intermediate proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Excel, Word, PowerPoint) Intermediate proficiency using Cashnet system. Customer service-oriented. Excellent organizational and communication skills required Ability to learn, communicate, and apply new systems and processes Excellent attention to detail, time management, and the ability to multi-task in a fast pace-environment Excellent follow-through skills, highly organized, flexible, and attentive to deadlines and priorities Ability to maintain confidentiality Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5475147/simulation-technology-specialist": {
      "title": "Simulation Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Simulation Technology Specialist Salary $65,000.00 - $70,000.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00292 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 09/08/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Responsible for nursing and interdisciplinary student simulation education and related program support, equipment management, and content development and delivery. Work closely with nursing faculty, students, and other stakeholders to ensure that simulation-based learning experiences are effective and aligned with educational goals. Note: The hours for this position are 11:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. Monday thru Friday. Duties and Responsibilities Conduct preventive maintenance checks and services of simulation equipment and troubleshoot and resolve technical issues. Prepare, maintain, and troubleshoot technical and mechanical aspects of the simulators and exam rooms, including the maintenance, cleaning, and reporting of any required repairs. Attain mastery of simulator operations software and a comprehensive knowledge of hardware characteristics, including coordinating with vendors to resolve serious mechanical failures. Install software updates on computers and maintain manikin components as directed by manufacturer support. Collaborate with Information Technology and simulation system vendors to install software updates and identify and isolate simulation system and network-related issues. Follows up on ticket resolutions. (35%) Assist in inventory of consumable and equipment supplies and restocking labs and simulation space as needed. Responsible for the proper setup, reset, operation, breakdown, storage, and technical support of simulation systems, computers, sim space, manikins, and supplies. Provide theatrical production (costuming and Moulage) for simulation scenarios as needed. Coordinate activities in the Control Room and operate simulators, task trainers, and the audio-visual equipment. Capture, edit, and replay simulation sessions for debriefing. (35%) Assist in the development and implementation of simulation education courses and experiences. Support faculty with open lab or remediation hours as needed. Attend industry conferences and participate in the continuing education professional development to stay current on the rapidly evolving simulation technology education. (15%) Assist faculty in the development, testing, and implementation of detailed clinically based simulation scenarios. Support professional staff with special projects, tours of the building, and in-person special events as needed. (10%) Collect data for ongoing quality improvements, research, or grant requirements. (5%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Associate’s degree in technology or a health-related field from an accredited institution required. One to three years’ experience working with simulation technologies (Laerdal and Gaumard) in a nursing or clinical education setting or experience in healthcare practice and will to learn simulation or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Two years’ experience in a related environment preferred. Experience in an academic, clinical, or medical setting preferred. Basic simulation equipment experience. Intermediate experience with Microsoft Office. Basic knowledge of medical terminology or willingness to be trained. Excellent organizational skills. Ability to effectively and independently coordinate multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Ability to adapt to and take full advantage of changing technology in nursing simulation. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about May require standing for extended periods of time. Ability to lift 20 lbs., or horizontally moving up to 150 lbs., of equipment DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5475908/open-rank-professor-of-elementary-education-methods": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Professor of Elementary Education Methods",
      "description": "Open-Rank Professor of Elementary Education Methods Salary See Position Description Location Providence College Job Type Ordinary Faculty Job Number PC00294 Division Academic Affairs Department Elementary and Special Education Opening Date 09/09/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview The Elementary/Special Education Department at Providence College invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, tenure-track faculty position in Elementary Education Methods, beginning in Fall 2027. We seek a scholar and educator who will contribute to the department’s commitment to academic excellence, evidence-based instructional practices, and the preparation of highly effective elementary and special education teachers. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring undergraduate teacher candidates, scholarship and professional engagement, and collaboration with schools and community partners. We particularly welcome candidates with an established or emerging research agenda that has the potential to enhance the department’s national visibility and contribute meaningfully to the field of elementary education and teacher preparation. As our student body, and Elementary Special Education majors, grow increasingly diverse; we have a strong preference for candidates who show a commitment to publicly engaged scholarship, student-centered pedagogical and mentoring practices, and support the success of students from historically marginalized economic, social, and cultural groups in the college classroom and in partner schools. Potential areas of specialization include but are not limited to social studies pedagogy, urban education, educating multilingual learners, inclusive systems and practices, and student teaching supervision. Providence College: Founded in 1917, Providence College (PC) is a premier Catholic liberal arts institution steadfastly committed to academic excellence through a dynamic core curriculum, a distinctive Development of Western Civilization Program, and abundant experiential learning opportunities. The only U.S. higher education institution administered by the Dominican Friars, PC is committed to providing a variety of opportunities for intellectual, social, moral, and spiritual growth in a supportive environment. Providence College believes that cultural and intellectual pluralism is essential to the excellence of its academic programs and strives to foster an academic culture and campus community reflecting the global environment in which we live and work. The approximately 105-acre campus is situated in Rhode Island’s capital city and is close to the many cultural and educational offerings of Rhode Island’s “renaissance city.” Additionally, Providence is located an hour from Boston and just a few hours from New York City. For years, Providence College has been recognized #1 in the U.S. News & World Report “Regional Universities – North Category” and is ranked #1 in Undergraduate Teaching. The School of Education and Social Work: The Department of Elementary Special Education is situated within the School of Education and Social Work (SESW). The School of Education and Social Work’s vision statement is that “Our graduates cultivate human flourishing and foster a more just society.” The SESW values Reflection, Inclusivity, Engagement and Excellence. https://education-social-work.providence.edu/ The Elementary/ Special Education Department: The Department of Education is widely recognized for its merged dual certification elementary and special education program. We seek to: a) educate and inclusively prepare outstanding pre-service teacher candidates in both elementary education (grades k-6) and special education (grades k-8); b) engage in high-quality teaching, scholarship, and service; and c) engage in diverse partnerships within our local community, across Rhode Island, throughout the New England Region and Internationally. The Elementary Special Education Program has a long history of emphasizing inclusive education, collaboration, and evidence-based practices. Salary: $69,000-$120,000 Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach face-to-face undergraduate elementary education methods courses and supervise associated field experiences. Design, develop, and deliver high-quality instructional, field-based learning experiences, and assessments. Advise Elementary/Special Education majors on coursework, including requirements within the Providence College Core Curriculum. Establish and maintain collaborative relationships with local schools and community partners. Contribute to accreditation and continuous program improvement activities. Participate actively in departmental and College-wide service and committee work. Develop and sustain a productive program of scholarly inquiry and disseminate research through appropriate professional and scholarly venues. Contribute to the College’s strategic priorities and mission through teaching, scholarship, service, and engagement with the broader community. Education and Experience Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in elementary education, teacher education, curriculum and instruction, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. ABD candidates may be considered, provided the doctorate is completed by the time of employment. Demonstrated record of, or clear potential for, scholarly activity and research related to elementary education, teacher preparation, or a closely related field. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and teacher preparation. Strong interpersonal, communication, and collaborative skills. Expertise in, or demonstrated interest in, one or more foundational elementary subject areas; expertise in social studies is particularly welcome. Prior professional teaching experience in K–6 elementary classrooms. Preferred Qualifications Experience with curriculum development, accreditation, program assessment, or other forms of academic program leadership. Experience teaching undergraduate students, particularly in teacher preparation programs. Experience collaborating with K–12 schools, districts, community organizations, or other educational partners. Evidence of engagement with evidence-based instructional practices and contemporary issues in elementary education. Supplemental Information For priority consideration, please submit all application materials by November 30, 2026. Instructions to candidates : Applicants should apply online at the College’s career site at https://careers.providence.edu and submit the following: Cover letter outlining qualifications Curriculum vitae Teaching statement/philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness Graduate transcripts Three letters of recommendation. If selected for an on-campus interview, candidate will be asked to respond to the college’s Mission Statement For additional information about the position, please contact Dr. Marcy Zipke, Chair, Elementary/Special Education Department, Providence College, Providence, RI 02918-0001 , at mzipke@providence.edu NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5480050/technology-service-audio-video-support-specialist": {
      "title": "Technology Service & Audio Video Support Specialist",
      "description": "Technology Service & Audio Video Support Specialist Salary $21.50 - $22.50 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Temporary Staff Job Number PC00300 Division Finance and Business Department Information Technology Opening Date 09/11/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Provide primary support for all media production and computer technology located in academic, administrative, and events spaces. This position also provide functional redundancy to the Technology Services & Application Support Specialists. Duties and Responsibilities Ensure that all classroom and event spaces function properly and are continuously ready for use by the college community. Respond to high priority tickets placed for instructional technology support in classrooms and labs to prevent class disruption. Ensure the timely processing of event requests for media presentations. (25%) In conjunction with Service Desk management, coordinate with student staff on the setup and operation of on-site media equipment event support and event recordings. Manage audio and video production, mixing, and audio and video recording of on-site events. Troubleshoot integration and operational problems. Assign and integrate appropriate equipment for the task and operate equipment when necessary. (20%) Assist faculty, staff, and visiting presenters on use of endpoint technology (laptops, tablets, phones, etc.), as well as presentation media equipment (projectors, Crestron devices, solstice pods, Apple TV’s, etc.) and troubleshoot problems during presentations. Assist the faculty and other users in specific media hardware or software related presentations. (20%) Provide support for other related IT staff in the field and verify issues prior to escalation. Assist with the network configuration of devices including working with system administrators when deploying new technologies and network upgrades as well as troubleshooting server and/or network access issues on devices. Assist faculty and staff with support of non-standard applications and assess if the problem is related to computer, network, or AV infrastructure. (15%) Assist Technology Services & Application Support Specialists in support of institutionally owned hardware of all types. Assist with the deployment of computers, networking cables, and configuration of space when upgrading existing labs and new deployments. Assist with performing hardware repairs as needed on all endpoints including computers, tablets, and printers. (10%) Serve as an escalation point for the Helpdesk Support Specialist as well as IT student workers, especially with walk-in tickets. Provide support for both standard and complex hardware and software issues. Track common issues and document solutions using Team Dynamix and other supported systems. Share documentation with other technicians as well as Helpdesk Support Specialists so more issues are resolved on first contact. Create self-service knowledge base articles for Team Dynamix. (10%) MARGINAL DUTIES: 1. Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Associate’s, vocational, or technical school degree from an accredited institution required. Bachelor’s degree preferred. One to three years’ experience working in a technology support position. Intermediate experience with media presentation technology and video editing. Basic knowledge of endpoint computer technology. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5482436/shift-supervisor-sergeant": {
      "title": "Shift Supervisor/Sergeant",
      "description": "Shift Supervisor/Sergeant Salary $69,000.00 - $75,000.00 Annually Location Providence College Job Type Full-time Staff Job Number PC00303 Division Student Affairs Department Public Safety Opening Date 09/15/2026 FLSA Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Oversee the protection of the college community and the protection of private and institutional property on the campus. Duties and Responsibilities Supervise all public safety officers and personnel under their command ensuring all are present and accounted for. Conduct a roll call at the beginning of each shift, and direct public safety functions under their command. May serve as incident commander on a critical incident. Ability to send out emergency messages. Monitor the activities and capabilities of their subordinates to ensure they are executing their duties and functions in a satisfactory manner that conforms to guidelines and directives in a professional, fair, and impartial manner. Evaluate subordinates and take remedial action when necessary. (65%) Supervise all Public Safety Officers assigned to special details and college events. Ensure that all personnel report to their post or detail and that all college policies are respected. (15%) Maintain public safety related equipment during their respective shift to include inspecting equipment including patrol vehicle components as related to safe and reliable operation. (10%) Supervise and direct the field training of all newly hired public safety officers under their command. Review and submit detailed, written progress reports to the FTO Coordinator. (5%) Subject to the approval of a higher authority, schedule work assignments, vacations, days off, training, etc., for personnel assigned to their respective shifts. (5%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree in criminal justice from an accredited institution required. Three to five years of police or security-related experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Excellent oral and written communication experience required. First aid and CPR certifications preferred. Computer literacy, including experience with Microsoft Suite (Word, Excel, etc.) Valid driver’s license required. Must be able to operate a vehicle and patrol campus Ability to multi-task and prioritize assignments. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Must successfully complete a background check, psychological testing, and physical agility pre-employment testing. Availability to work all shifts Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about Designated as essential emergency personnel DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Providence College offers a comprehensive range of valuable benefits to eligible employees, which are designed to: Promote the health and well-being of you and your family Provide financial security while you are working Build financial resources for retirement Help you balance personal and work responsibilities Provide educational opportunities for you and your family These benefits include but are not limited to health, dental, 403b retirement plan, flexible benefits plan, tuition benefits, employee assistance plan, college paid basic life insurance and long-term disability insurance, and paid time off. To learn more, please visit our Employee Benefits website by clicking the following link: https://human-resources.providence.edu/benefits/ Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
