    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/providencecollege/jobs/5485781/psychiatric-nurse-practitioner": {
      "title": "Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner Salary $90.00 - $100.00 Hourly Location Providence College Job Type Part-time Staff Job Number PC00305 Division Student Affairs Department Personal Counseling Opening Date 09/17/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit NU Description Benefits Conducted under the auspices of the Dominican Friars, Providence College is a Catholic, Dominican, liberal arts institution of higher education and a community committed to academic excellence in pursuit of the truth, growth in virtue, and service of God and neighbor. We seek candidates who can affirm and contribute to our mission. Providence College is also an equal opportunity employer and is committed to fostering a Beloved Community — an environment that reflects the rich diversity of the human family and is marked by justice, charity and the promotion of the common good and flourishing of all. We invite applications from qualified individuals who possess the experience, knowledge and commitment to develop the diverse learning environment envisioned as part of the Beloved Community. Women and minority candidates are strongly encouraged to apply. The College’s Non-Discrimination policy can be found Notice of Non-Discrimination (PDF document) Overview Assesses, diagnoses, and treats mental health conditions via comprehensive psychiatric evaluations and medication management to support mental health, academic functioning, and well-being of students referred by Personal Counseling Center Staff. This is a part-time and academic year (9-month) position. Duties and Responsibilities Provide psychiatric evaluations, assessment, and medication management services to students presenting a wide range of mental health concerns. Provide detailed education on risks/benefits of medications and interactions with other prescribed or recreational substances. Develop comprehensive treatment planning for caseload, including assisting with appropriate referrals for medication management when students are away from campus for continuity of care. Monitor medication adherence, side effects, and treatment outcomes using best practices. (75%) Collaborate with internal and external treatment providers to coordinate comprehensive care, including consultation with the contracted psychiatrist and case discussions with counseling and health services staff. Meet with the executive director periodically to review cases of concern and flow of system. (10%) Partner with health Services and Sports Medicine staff (Athletic team doctors) to coordinate laboratory testing, as needed cardiac testing, and review medical concerns related to psychiatric treatment. Communicate clearly about medication interactions and health monitoring needs. Consult with both departments, as needed. (5%) Assist in referral management for higher or specialized care, including partial hospitalization, emergency referrals for inpatient level of care assessment, intensive outpatient programs, or off-campus psychiatric providers. Ensure appropriate handoff and continuity of care. (5%) Provide timely documentation in the electronic medical records system within the Personal Counseling Center’s policies and procedures, following state and institutional standards. Utilize EMR systems in Health Services and Athletics for electronic prescription services. Provide documentation for varsity student athletes when needed for NCAA mandates related to controlled substances. (5%) MARGINAL DUTIES: Perform all other duties as may be required. Education and Experience Master of Science in Nursing from an accredited institution required. One to three years’ hands-on experience, preferable in a higher education counseling center or an equivalent combination of education and experience. APRN license in the State of Rhode Island. Current board certification as a Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP-BC) from the ANNC (American Nurses Credentialing Center). Rhode Island Controlled Substances Registration (CSR license)/Federal DEA Registration. Intermediate proficiency with electronic medical records systems. Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite Ability to provide intricate substance use assessments to assess dual/comorbid diagnoses, level of risk regarding substance use, and potential prescribed medications in college population. Experience working with assessing for disordered eating/eating disorders given the higher occurrence in a higher education setting. Ability to work effectively in a team-based setting that requires flexibility based on potential for emergency/risk assessments while also being able to work independently. Strong communication and interpersonal skills to provide complex diagnostic and treatment feedback to students. Minimum of one year post board certification. College mental health experience preferred, but not required. Supplemental Information PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Sitting in a normal seated position for extended periods of time Reaching by extending hand(s) or arm(s) in any direction Finger dexterity required to manipulate objects with fingers rather than with whole hand(s) or arm(s), for example, using a keyboard Communication skills using the spoken word Ability to see within normal parameters Ability to hear within normal range Ability to move about DISCLAIMER: This job description indicates the general nature and level of work expected of the incumbent. It is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities required of the incumbent. Incumbent may be asked to perform other duties as required. NOTICE OF E-VERIFY PARTICIPATION Providence College participates in E-Verify to confirm the identity and employment authorization of individuals hired to work in the United States. Before submitting this application, please review the following documents: E-Verify Notice of Participation Right to Work By continuing with this application, you acknowledge that you have been informed of our participation in E-Verify and have had the opportunity to review these notices. Part-time employees are eligible for the College’s meal plan discount, Working Advantage discount, Rhode Island’s Sick and Safe Leave, and voluntary 403(b) retirement plan contributions. Employer Providence College (RI) Address 1 Cunningham Square Providence, Rhode Island, 02918-0001 Phone (401) 865-2341 Website www.providence.edu Apply"
